---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Portrait from "../components/Portrait.astro";
import CtaLink from "../components/CtaLink.astro";
import { site, availability } from "../site";
---

<Base>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 pt-14 sm:px-6 md:pt-20">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-8 md:flex-row md:items-start md:gap-12">
      <Portrait class="h-24 w-24 shrink-0 md:h-32 md:w-32" />
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-5xl leading-[1.05] md:text-6xl">Hey, I'm {site.firstName}.</h1>
        <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-xl leading-relaxed">
          I build websites for Charlotte restaurants and small businesses, and I help owners make sense of their
          numbers. Most people who do one can't do the other. I do both, and you deal with me the whole way.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
          <CtaLink href="/contact/" variant="secondary">Book a {availability.callMinutes}-minute video call</CtaLink>
          <a href="#what" class="font-semibold underline decoration-accent decoration-2 underline-offset-4">What I do</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="what" class="mx-auto mt-20 max-w-5xl scroll-mt-8 px-4 sm:px-6">
    <h2 class="text-3xl">Pick what you need</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 grid border-y border-line md:grid-cols-3 md:divide-x md:divide-line">
      <a href="/pixel/" class="group border-b border-line py-8 md:border-b-0 md:pr-8">
        <p class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold text-accent">Pixel</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg">
          A website that lets customers book, order or find your hours without calling you.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">From $1,800, then $95 a month to keep it running.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 font-semibold group-hover:underline">See Pixel →</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/tally/" class="group border-b border-line py-8 md:border-b-0 md:px-8">
        <p class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold text-accent-2">Tally</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg">
          Your sales, labor and bookings on one page, so you know which nights and items actually make money.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">A checkup is $300. A live dashboard is $1,500.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 font-semibold group-hover:underline">See Tally →</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/both/" class="group py-8 md:pl-8">
        <p class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold">Both</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg">
          The site brings in the bookings. The numbers tell you what they're worth. One person handles both.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">Starter Site and a Data Checkup together for $1,950.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 font-semibold group-hover:underline">See Both →</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto mt-20 grid max-w-5xl gap-10 px-4 sm:px-6 md:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr]">
    <h2 class="text-3xl">How I work</h2>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        We start with a short call. You tell me what's annoying you, whether that's missed calls, an old site, or not
        knowing if Tuesdays are worth staying open. I tell you what I'd do and what it costs.
      </p>
      <p>
        You get the price in writing before I start, and it doesn't change. You can text me while I work, and when it's
        done I walk you through it. If you want, I keep it running for a monthly fee you can cancel any time.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted">
        I'm new to doing this on my own, so there are no client reviews here yet, and I'm not going to make any up.
        My first three clients get 15% off in exchange for an honest one.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
